ategory="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5645143-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5645143</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1035346A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKEBONO BRAKE IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKEBONO RES &amp; DEV CENTRE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKEBONO BRAKE INDUSTRY CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKEBONO RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT CENTRE LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGAWA YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p> A disc brake (1) for allowing a piston (9) in a cylinder (13) to press friction pads (5, 6) against a rotor (3) by means of an oil pressure supplied to a caliper body (7), wherein an electric oil pressure generator (15) is incorporated in the caliper body (7) with a solid element capable of controlling electrically an expansion/contraction operation used as a drive source and is connected to the cylinder (13) via an oil passage (29) formed in the caliper body (7), thereby eliminating the need of an oil pressure pipeline between a cylinder on the caliper body and the electric oil pressure generator and enhancing the operational accuracy and maintainability of the disc brake.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un frein (1) à disque conçu pour permettre au piston (9) d'un cylindre (13) d'appliquer des patins (5, 6) de frein contre un rotor (3) par pression hydraulique délivrée à un compas (7). Un générateur (15) électrique de pression hydraulique incorporé dans le compas (7) comporte un élément monobloc capable de commander électriquement un mouvement de déploiement/télescopage servant de source motrice. Ce générateur raccordé au cylindre (13) par un passage (29) hydraulique formé dans le compas (7) évite d'utiliser un conduit hydraulique entre le cylindre du compas et le générateur, la précision de fonctionnement et la maintenabilité du frein à disque étant ainsi améliorées.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>